<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry III, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1016–1056</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Henry the Black</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry III, of the Salian dynasty, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1039 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1046. At the Synod of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutri">Sutri</a> in 1046 he deposed rival popes and went on to install reforming German popes. He favoured the palace at Goslar, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rammelsberg">Rammelsberg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines, where he founded the collegiate church of Saints Simon and Jude; his heart was buried there after his death in 1056.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Henry III, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="700" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown painterUnknown painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_III._(HRR)_Miniatur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
